+## QUALITY
+
+### Code quality
+
+The count fix is the minimal correct one and is ordered correctly — the existence test runs **before**
+`cp -pR`, so it observes the pre-copy state rather than the file it is about to create:
+
+```
+  if [ ! -e "$taxonomy_target" ] && [ ! -L "$taxonomy_target" ]; then
+    files=$((files + 1))
+  fi
+  cp -pR "$taxonomy_from" "$taxonomy_target"
+```
+
+The `|| -L` half matters: a dangling symlink at the destination is a path that already exists but
+that plain `-e` reports absent, which would have re-introduced the same over-count in a different
+shape. It mirrors the guard already used at `:78`. No dead code, no duplication, no new branch left
+untested.
+
+### No regression
+
+Nothing was removed or re-signed. The script change is four lines inside one existing `if`; the test
+change is additive. The whole suite is green on the merged tree (see INTEGRATION), and the two
+neighbouring behaviours the fixture change could have disturbed — the default file count and the
+"does not carry untracked files" case — both still pass.
